# Negative-control mutant — the collection's criteria schema owns ALL request
# state (R38 item 13, supersedes R28/R32's pagination-only ruling): filters,
# sort AND pagination reach the wire only through `list({ criteria: { schema } })`.
# No task/spec basename named this control yet — R38 (2026-09-28) postdates
# `tasks.md`; this patch is authored against the ruling directly, for the
# prover to anchor a schema-validation spec to.
#
# NOT PROVEN (FE-3145): no driven scenario goes red under this mutant. Only a
#   full-directory run turned contract.traceability.test.ts red; that file run
#   alone stays green, so no scenario pins this behaviour yet.
#
# Mutation: `useQuerySchema`'s top-level `additionalProperties` flips from
#   `false` to `true`, so an AJV validation against the schema silently admits
#   any extra top-level key instead of rejecting it — the schema no longer
#   OWNS the request state, it merely describes part of it.
#
# Apply with:  git apply <this file>   (run from repo root)
# Revert with: git apply -R <this file>
